    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as our definitive anchor, boasting an elite 80.40 score despite facing a tough matchup against Kirby. His high projection is driven by a massive +16% park adjustment that helps negate the SP skill penalty, combined with an ideal #2 spot in the order. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** offers a potent high-ceiling play at 74.38; his efficiency is bolstered by a favorable 4.46 xERA for Singer and a strong +13% platoon edge, making him a primary target for counting stats today. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (63.17) and **Kyle Tucker** (64.59) remain in our \"Strong\" tier, their contributions are essential for maintaining our core offensive floor against the respective arms of Luzardo and Jones.\n\nStrategic benching remains a tight margin for the Waves, with **Miguel Vargas** (42.35) serving as the most difficult omission. His score was dragged down significantly by a -19% SP skill penalty against the formidable Sale, pushing him below the threshold compared to the platoon-advantaged **Nasim Nunez** (58.52) and **Wade Meckler** (57.49). We are keeping a close eye on **Liam Hicks** (58.72); while he earns his spot through a +11% dynamic platoon advantage and a leadoff order boost, the 4.45 xERA of Nelson suggests a volatility risk that keeps him just below the elite tier. \n\nWe must emphasize situational awareness regarding our speed-focused roster depth, especially given the scarcity of stolen bases. **Nasim Nunez** and **Wade Meckler** are leveraged today specifically for their efficiency and order positioning, as we prioritize maximizing plate appearances over raw power. Be advised that we are monitoring the bottom of the order, specifically **Brayan Rocchio** (49.09) and **Dominic Smith** (49.27), as these players hover near the marginal floor. Should any weather or late lineup shifts materialize, we are prepared to pivot to our bench, though we remain hampered by the continued absence of **Jordan Westburg** and **Jacob Wilson** on the IL.",
